                    <birth when="1751-11-14">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1824-05-26"/>
                    <occupation>editor</occupation>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Lofft was a radical who was involved in the movement to repeal the Test and Corporation Acts in the late 1780s and early 1790s. He was a stern critic
of the Pitt regime, a noted campaigner against the death penalty, and was a prolific author.</p>
                        <p>See the letter from Lofft in the Abinger Papers,  for June 1803.</p>
                        <p>Godwin records his death.</p>
                    </note>
